## 13. Integration with MedOrbits

Recommended dependency direction:

```text
API / Web Layer
      |
      v
Application Services
      |
      +----> Validation Utilities
      +----> Configuration
      +----> Logging
      +----> Import / Export
      +----> Health Checks
      |
      v
Repositories / External Integrations
      |
      +----> Database
      +----> Email Provider
      +----> Queue / Redis
      +----> Storage
      +----> Payment Provider
      +----> AI Provider
```

Keep the package independent of HTTP request objects and framework-specific response types. Convert `ValidationError` and health reports into API responses at the web layer.

If MedOrbits also uses a Node.js backend, keep the Python package's environment variable names, schemas, database settings, and error contracts aligned with the Node implementation.

